{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4e988a0bb03a6d2","type":"tool_result","content":"     262 .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/eval-hub.md\n     232 .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kube-rbac-proxy.md\n     628 .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md\n     363 .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/trustyai-service.md\n    1485 total\n# Component: eval-hub\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/eval-hub.git\n- **Version**: d043d23f6336f41e7508137fed1c46b52a65ecf6\n- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n- **Languages**: Go\n- **Deployment Type**: Application Service\n- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n\n## Purpose\n\n**Short**: Eval-hub is an evaluation orchestration service for RHOAI that manages evaluation jobs, collections, and providers through a REST API, coordinating with Kubernetes batch Jobs, MLflow tracking, S3-compatible storage, and OpenTelemetry for observability. [source: internal/eval_hub/server/server.go:444, internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:24, cmd/eval_runtime_init/main.go:114, internal/otel/otel_sdk.go:174]\n\n**Detailed**: Eval-hub provides a centralized evaluation orchestration service for Red Hat OpenShift AI. The primary server (`eval_hub`) exposes a REST API on port 8080 with endpoints for managing evaluation jobs, collections, and providers, protected by conditional identity header enforcement (X-User/X-Tenant) when enabled by configuration. A dedicated Prometheus metrics server runs on port 8081 in cluster mode. The service coordinates evaluation workloads by creating Kubernetes batch Jobs, ConfigMaps, and Secrets via client-go, and manages HardwareProfile custom resources for hardware-aware scheduling. It integrates with MLflow for experiment tracking via a TLS-configured HTTP client, S3-compatible storage for test data via AWS SDK, and exports traces/metrics to an OpenTelemetry Collector over OTLP/gRPC. The `eval_runtime_sidecar` acts as a proxy for evaluation runtime containers, `eval_runtime_init` handles S3 test-data downloads as an init container, and `evalhub_mcp` provides a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server interface. All Go binaries are built with `CGO_ENABLED=1` and `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` for FIPS compliance on UBI9. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:27-52, internal/eval_hub/server/server.go:444, internal/eval_hub/config/prometheus.go:4, internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:112-232]\n\n## Architectural Analysis\n\nEval-hub follows a multi-process architecture where the main API server orchestrates evaluation workloads through Kubernetes batch primitives. The `setupRoutes` function at `server.go:444` registers route groups for evaluation jobs, collections, providers, health, and documentation, all behind a conditional identity enforcement middleware that checks `X-User` and `X-Tenant` headers when the `RequiresIdentityHeaders()` configuration flag is set—bypassed entirely in local/development mode (`server.go:430-441`). This configuration-gated authentication model means that identity enforcement depends on the deployment configuration rather than being structurally guaranteed, which is a meaningful security consideration for platform operators.\n\nThe Kubernetes interaction layer in `KubernetesHelper` (`k8s_helper.go`) provides CRUD operations across ConfigMaps, Secrets, Jobs, and HardwareProfile custom resources (`infrastructure.opendatahub.io/v1`). Evaluation workloads are dispatched as Kubernetes batch Jobs, with ConfigMaps carrying evaluation configurations and Secrets holding credentials. The HardwareProfile CRD integration enables hardware-aware scheduling of evaluation workloads.\n\nThe service maintains optional integrations with MLflow for experiment tracking (`mlflow.go:43-92`), constructing an HTTP client with TLS 1.2-1.3 enforcement and optional custom CA certificate loading. The MLflow client is nil-safe—when no tracking URI is configured, the server starts without MLflow integration. Storage uses pluggable SQL backends (SQLite for local development, PostgreSQL for production), with the database schema managed through the `internal/eval_hub/storage/sql` package.\n\nNo Kubernetes Service or ingress manifests exist in this repository; service exposure is platform-delegated, consistent with the `io.openshift.expose-services=\"\"` label in the Dockerfile. The metrics server runs on a separate port (default 8081) in cluster mode, while in local mode `/metrics` is also served on the main API port for development convenience (`server.go:470-477`).\n\n## Provenance\n\n### Repo Lineage\n\n| Role | Repository | Sync Mechanism | Sync Branch | Sync Workflows | Detection Method |\n|----|----------|--------------|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n| Upstream | https://github.com/opendatahub-io/eval-hub | auto_merge | main | -- | sync_config |\n| Downstream | https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/eval-hub | auto_merge | main | `check-trustyai-service-operator-configmap-sync.yml`, `sync-branch-incubation.yaml`, `sync-branch-stable.yaml` | local_analysis |\n\n### Aliases\n\n| Current Name | Previous Name | Type | Context |\n|------------|-------------|----|-------|\n\n## Architecture Components\n\n| Component | Type | Purpose |\n|---------|----|-------|\n| Dockerfile.konflux:CMD | Container entrypoint | [\"/app/eval-hub\"] |\n| Metrics Server | HTTP Service | Standalone Prometheus metrics service backed by a runtime HTTP listener |\n| eval_hub | Go executable | cmd/eval_hub |\n| eval_runtime_init | Go executable | cmd/eval_runtime_init |\n| eval_runtime_sidecar | Go executable | cmd/eval_runtime_sidecar |\n| evalhub_mcp | Go executable | cmd/evalhub_mcp |\n| validate_configs | Go executable | cmd/validate_configs |\n\n## APIs Exposed\n\n### Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)\n\n| Group | Version | Kind | Scope | API Role | Purpose |\n|-----|-------|----|-----|--------|-------|\n\n### Serving Runtime Definitions\n\n| Name | Kind | API Group | Version | Scope | Supported Model Formats | Container Images | Built-in Adapter | Source |\n|----|----|---------|-------|-----|-----------------------|----------------|----------------|------|\n\n### HTTP Endpoints\n\n| Path | Method | Port | Protocol | Transport | Encryption | Auth | Owner | Purpose |\n|----|------|----|--------|---------|----------|----|-----|-------|\n| / | Unknown |  | HTTP | HTTP/1.1 | Unknown | Unknown | internal/evalhub_mcp/server | Registered Go HTTP route |\n| /health | Unknown |  | HTTP | HTTP/1.1 | Unknown | Unknown | internal/evalhub_mcp/server | Registered Go HTTP route |\n| /metrics | Unknown |  | HTTP | HTTP/1.1 | Unknown | Unknown | internal/eval_hub/server | Registered Go HTTP route |\n\n### gRPC Services\n\n| Service | Port | Protocol | Transport | Encryption | Auth | Owner | Purpose |\n|-------|----|--------|---------|----------|----|-----|-------|\n\n## Dependencies","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85a41162facd59f","agent_id":"a6de3a8d673d618fd","session_id":"f780de70-496a-445e-b2ff-c0c509886095","uuid":"1e584802-3cdb-4f61-8d9b-699c6861ca0b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:40:13.638Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4e988a0bb03a6d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
