{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-590576d5-aeda-44c5-a28e-abe67c5656e4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95e066dadd6ea442","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-kyg0mt8n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8005 — EvalHub UI: Real-Time Evaluation Job Progress and State Visibility\n\n## Triage Outcome\n\nThe strategy is S-sized, single-active-component (eval-hub-ui plugin), and single-team (ODH Dashboard), but the below-threshold path does **not** apply: the strategy's Open Questions table contains two genuine unknowns explicitly marked \"needs validation\" in the Assumptions section — (1) whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated in the detail endpoint response while a job is still running, and (2) whether `status.message.message_code` reliably distinguishes pre-start failures from runtime failures. Per Step 6.5, strategy-flagged open questions are genuine unknowns and must not be downgraded to implementation details. The answer to (1) determines whether the detail-polling layer, benchmark-level progress display, and `started_at`-based elapsed time are implementable as specified (a change to what the implementation epic does); the answer to (2) determines whether the P2 pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction is implementable. Full decomposition proceeds.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input (Step 1.5)\n\nThe Staff Engineer Input section is non-empty and was parsed first; it takes precedence. It is consistent with the AI-generated Technical Approach (the strategy was already adjusted to it), so no divergences required override logging. Directions incorporated from Staff Engineer Input:\n\n- No data beyond the two existing API endpoints (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs`, `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) is assumed; the plan is built on what those endpoints actually return