{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d2b57a61-4bb1-43e0-a026-b73f104a6c0f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98c0ae5230798ed2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-kyg0mt8n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E002.md","content":"# Progress indicator and state differentiation UX specification for the EvalHub Evaluations page\n\n## Description\n\nAuthor the progress indicator UX specification listed as \"to be created\" in the strategy's Supporting Documentation. This epic produces the design specification the EvalHub UI implementation builds against: state icon/color specifications and the progress indicator pattern for the Evaluations landing page job table, aligned to PatternFly components and the dashboard design system. It covers the UXD Support prerequisite the strategy marks as required (\"progress indicator pattern, state icon/color specs\").\n\n## Scope\n\n- State visual differentiation specifications for the four job states derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field — Queued/Pending, Running, Failed, Completed — with a distinct PatternFly icon, color, and label per state.\n- Failure-state variants: specification for \"Failed (not started)\" versus runtime \"Failed\" where the API's `message_code` data permits the distinction, plus the fallback treatment (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail) when it does not.\n- Progress indicator pattern for running jobs: elapsed time as the primary indicator for all jobs (per the strategy's mitigation for single-benchmark coarseness), with benchmark count (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") as supplementary where available.\n- Non-blocking warning presentation for temporarily unavailable status updates (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") shown alongside the last successfully fetched data.\n- The specification is written to cover both possible outcomes of the API data-availability validation (benchmark progress available mid-run, or not), so it does not require rework either way.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Specification defines icon, color, and label treatments for all four states, visually distinguishable from one another per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- Specification defines the progress indicator pattern with elapsed time as primary indicator and benchmark count as supplementary, including behavior for single-benchmark jobs where X/N is coarse.\n- Specification defines the non-blocking warning banner treatment for stale status data.\n- Specification covers both the pre-start/runtime failure distinction and its fallback treatment.\n- Specification is reviewed and agreed with the ODH Dashboard team implementing the Evaluations page.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0) — visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states: this epic produces the icon/color/label specifications.\n- HLR-4 (P1), HLR-5 (P1) — benchmark-level progress and elapsed time display: this epic produces the progress indicator pattern the implementation follows.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46619,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85a41162facd59f","agent_id":"a6de3a8d673d618fd","session_id":"f780de70-496a-445e-b2ff-c0c509886095","uuid":"a82d8818-cb88-4e43-87ca-07fc4ebcd143","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:43:49.490Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
