{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3d2aa9e0e8f143","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8005\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Completeness\n9\t  description: 'The strategy risk that the autorag React Query retry pattern is untested\n10\t    in the eval-hub Module Federation context (mitigation: validate in development\n11\t    by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF) is covered only implicitly by E003 5xx\n12\t    retry AC; add an explicit AC to validate the retry pattern against simulated BFF\n13\t    5xx responses.'\n14\terror: null\n15\t---\n16\t## Review Summary\n17\t\n18\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n19\tRecommendation: accept\n20\t\n21\t## Criterion Details\n22\t\n23\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n24\tAll seven HLRs (HLR-1 through HLR-7) appear in the traceability matrix and in at least one epic's \"HLR Traceability\" section: HLR-1/3/4/5/6/7 in E003, HLR-2 in both E002 (specification) and E003 (implementation). No P0 HLR is missing. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 and E002 are prerequisites of E003, which carries P0 HLRs, so both are correctly P0 — an epic gating P0 work must be P0. Priority collapse was considered and correctly rejected: the P1 HLRs (benchmark progress, elapsed time, Page Visibility pause) are intrinsic to the same detail-polling hook and job-table-row surface as the P0 auto-refresh and state-differentiation work, and the P2 pre-start failure distinction is a label variant on the same state-differentiation UI (incidental polish, not a deferrable sprint-scale feature). The decomposition documents this reasoning explicitly.\n25\t\n26\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n27\tDAG: E001 → E003 and E002 → E003, with E001 ∥ E002. Both edges in the mermaid diagram (drawn dependency → dependent, matching the `graph TD` convention) have matching entries in E003's frontmatter `dependencies`, and vice versa — no mismatch, no invalid references, no cycles. The E001 → E003 edge is a valid investigation gate (Rule 3): the validation outcome changes what E003 builds, recorded as `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001` on E003 with `gate_failure_impact` populated (action=rewrite plus a concrete fallback approach). The gated_by target appears in E003's direct dependencies. The E002 → E003 edge is a valid producer-consumer edge (UX specification as design contract; the strategy marks UXD Support as required for exactly these deliverables). The absence of an E001 → E002 edge is justified: the spec is scoped to cover both validation outcomes, so the two run in parallel — no unjustified serialization of parallel-eligible work. No konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist, so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are vacuous. No conditional branch files exist, and the decomposition justifies why (outcomes change E003's scope, not the structure — correctly handled as a rewrite gate). Critical path length 2 is within the S-size heuristic (1-2). Scanning epic content for uncaptured data/artifact dependencies found none — E003's only consumed artifacts (E001's findings, E002's spec) are both edged.\n28\t\n29\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n30\tThree epics with three distinct component/team tuples: E001 (AI Evaluations / TrustyAI-EvalHub), E002 (UXD / UX-Design), E003 (AI Core Dashboard / ODH Dashboard). All canonical component names verified against `.context/rhai-components.txt` (AI Core Dashboard, AI Evaluations, UXD all present); the mapping notes for the non-canonical strategy names (eval-hub-ui plugin, odh-dashboard BFF → AI Core Dashboard) are reasonable and documented. E003 does not span teams: the odh-dashboard BFF is a passive component (\"no code change expected\") owned by the same team, and its verification is correctly folded in as an acceptance criterion rather than a separate epic. No scope duplication between E002 and E003 — one produces the specification, the other implements it; that is a producer-consumer split, not duplicate building. No work-product type mixing: content authoring (the UX spec) is isolated in E002; E003's \"incidental documentation touch-ups\" are captions/references incidental to the code change, not content authoring. E003 is dense but the strategy itself estimates S (1-2 sprints, single team, \"constrained to a single hook\"), so it does not exceed the ~2-week epic bound.\n31\t\n32\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n33\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its two questions are marked \"needs validation\" in the strategy's Assumptions and Open Questions, and the answers change what E003 builds (benchmark-count progress vs. elapsed-time-only; pre-start failure distinction vs. single Failed state) — the outcome passes the \"changes downstream scope\" test. E001 has a downstream dependent (E003). E002 and E003 are Implementations producing concrete artifacts (a UX specification; the polling layer and UI). E003 correctly carries `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001` (it depends on an Investigation) with `gate_failure_impact.action` and `fallback_approach` both populated; a failure genuinely changes the epic's scope (rewrite), so this is a true gate, not a disguised scheduling dependency. E001 and E002 have no Investigation dependencies, so no missing gated_by. The gated_by target is in the direct dependencies list.\n34\t\n35\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n36\tEach epic carries the signal set matching its type: E001 has `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric), E002 and E003 have `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) — no type/rubric mismatch. E001: question_specificity 1 (two concrete, verbatim strategy questions), source_accessibility 1 (open Go repo plus published API reference — a factual source question, not a pending human decision), local_runnability 0 and cluster_hardware_dependence -1 (source analysis carries the answer; only peripheral empirical confirmation needs a cluster), human_judgment_required 0 (factual/technical questions) — all consistent with the strategy content. E002: change_specificity 0 (icon/color choices are the work product), open_questions 0 (spec scoped to cover both validation outcomes — the unresolved questions genuinely do not block design authoring), human_process_gates -1 (UXD review pending) — justified. E003: open_questions -1 correctly reflects the two unresolved gating questions (not the contradictory 1), change_specificity/pattern_precedent/adapter_pattern/existing_foundation/repo_access/architecture_claims all 1 with rationales matching the strategy's specific file, endpoint, and architecture-context citations. Rationales in all three ai-signals files match the frontmatter values. No arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n37\t\n38\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n39\tAll three epics have testable ACs derived from the strategy. E003's ACs directly adapt the strategy's seven proposed ACs (benchmark progress, 30s state-badge update, elapsed time, queued treatment, pre-start failure treatment with documented fallback, 5xx stale-data + warning + round-robin continuation with backoff, background-tab pause verified via dev tools) plus the concurrency cap, BFF passthrough, UX-spec conformance, and a green CI/build pipeline AC. Contingent ACs are explicitly annotated with the gate fallback rather than left ambiguous. E001's ACs require source-cited, enumerated answers with pass/fail conclusions. E002's ACs are concrete (all four states specified, single-benchmark behavior, warning treatment, fallback, review agreement). No rule-mandated ACs apply (no replacement/rollback epic — the change is additive; no docs-authoring epic; no konflux chain). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-references use full descriptions or frontmatter IDs.\n40\t\n41\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n42\tAll strategy scope is covered: two-layer polling, 10s cycle, max-5 round-robin concurrency, visible-page-only targeting with pagination retargeting, progress model with elapsed-time-primary, retry-on-error per the autorag pattern, Page Visibility pause/resume, state differentiation with message_code distinction and fallback, graceful degradation, BFF passthrough verification (AC on E003), and the \"to be created\" progress indicator UX specification (E002 — covering the UXD Support prerequisite). All seven strategy acceptance criteria appear in E003's AC list. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the two open questions drive E001, the single-benchmark coarseness risk mitigation (elapsed time primary) is in E003's scope and E002's spec scope, deferred scalability is documented as out of scope per Staff Engineer direction, and pending human process gates are reflected in E003's human_process_gates signal. Docs-authoring check: the strategy's Prerequisites list \"Documentation Support: _Pending human review_\", not \"Yes\", and the strategy requires no substantive doc content — the decomposition's justification for omitting a docs-authoring epic is sound. One minor nit: the strategy risk that the autorag React Query retry pattern is untested in the eval-hub Module Federation context (mitigation: validate in development by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF) is covered implicitly by E003's 5xx retry AC but is not carried as an explicit validation AC — incidental, does not affect execution correctness.\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93e6718f5d7b45b8","agent_id":"a9dd5f0457009ff6c","session_id":"f780de70-496a-445e-b2ff-c0c509886095","uuid":"2245cae4-dad2-4957-bba3-470039704304","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:50:02.011Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3d2aa9e0e8f143","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
