ules. No scope duplication between siblings: E002 authors the specification and E003 implements against it — a producer/consumer split along the work-product axis, not duplicate construction of the same surface. Work-product types are correctly separated: content/design authoring (E002) is its own epic, distinct from the code implementation (E003); the only authoring inside E003 is incidental doc touch-ups, which is acceptable. No epic exceeds ~2 weeks: the strategy is S-sized (1-2 sprints) and the single implementation epic is constrained to one plugin, one hook, and one table surface.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its two questions come verbatim from the strategy's Open Questions table (both marked \"needs validation\" in Assumptions), and the answers change what E003 builds (benchmark-count progress vs. elapsed-time-only; failure-class distinction vs. single Failed state) — a structural scope change, correctly modeled as a rewrite gate rather than a scheduling dependency. It has a downstream dependent (E003) and produces a findings report. E002 and E003 are Implementations producing concrete artifacts (the UX specification document; the polling layer and UI). Gating metadata is complete and consistent: E003 has `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001` with `gate_failure_impact` populated with both `action: rewrite` and a concrete `fallback_approach`, and the `gated_by` target appears in E003's direct `dependencies` list. E001 and E002 correctly have null `gated_by`. No epic lists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by`.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nSignal fields are type-appropriate on all three epics: E001 (Investigation) carries `investigation_signals` with null `ai_signals`; E002 and E003 (Implementation) carry `ai_signals` with null `investigation_signals`. All three ai-signals rationale files exist and their values match the frontmatter. Spot-checks against the strategy content: E003 `open_questio